// AddThree -- the Pyrope equivalent of verilog/AddThree.sv (DatapathBench).
//
// Hand-written, not emitted from the Verilog: a machine emission would enter
// the same LGraph the Verilog does and measure the two FRONT ENDS rather than
// the two languages. See [status].pyrope in design.toml.
//
// Ports keep the Verilog names and the widths of the pinned point (BW = 48),
// so the generated harness and LEC bind the same external interface.
//
// Three 48-bit operands can carry two bits past 48; the 49-bit result drops
// the top one, which `wrap` makes explicit.
pub comb AddThree(a:u48, b:u48, c:u48) -> (sum:u49) { wrap  sum = a + b + c }
